# PART 15 — AUCTION PSYCHOLOGY AND RIVAL REACTIONS

Implement strategic bidding psychology.

AI should analyze:

- User bidding patterns
- Aggressive bidding
- Frequent bidding
- Sudden withdrawal
- Budget remaining
- Preferred players
- Previous purchases
- User's squad weaknesses

AI may react strategically.

Examples:

- If the user repeatedly pursues fast bowlers, AI may compete for scarce premium fast bowlers.
- If the user has spent heavily, AI may stop competing against them.
- If a player is overvalued, AI may withdraw.
- If a franchise lacks a wicketkeeper, AI may prioritize one.
- If only a few death bowlers remain, AI may value them more highly.
- AI may avoid bidding wars when better alternatives are available.

Implement a bidding psychology system based on strategic logic.

Do not use paid AI APIs.

